rection</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">machine</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine\">Machine</a> <span class=\"fn\">dir</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine\">Machine</a> <span class=\"fn\">dir</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Advances reader-side state machine by one logical transition.\n\nDispatches parsing work according to current reader state (start-line, headers,\nbody, completion, or failure handling).","docLink":"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.processRead","kind":"opaque","line":1982,"name":"Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.processRead","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Protocol/H1.lean#L1982-L2006"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">partial def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.processWrite\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Protocol</span>.<span class=\"name\">H1</span>.<span class=\"name\">Machine</span>.<span class=\"name\">processWrite</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">dir</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Message.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Direction\">Direction</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">machine</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine\">Machine</a> <span class=\"fn\">dir</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine\">Machine</a> <span class=\"fn\">dir</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Advances writer-side state machine by one logical transition.\n\nDepending on writer state, this may:\n- request an application answer,\n- serialize headers,\n- flush fixed/chunked body bytes,\n- finalize/close after completion.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.processWrite","kind":"opaque","line":1468,"name":"Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.processWrite","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Protocol/H1.lean#L1468-L1507"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.takeOutput\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Protocol</span>.<span class=\"name\">H1</span>.<span class=\"name\">Machine</span>.<span class=\"name\">takeOutput</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">dir</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Message.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Direction\">Direction</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">machine</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine\">Machine</a> <span class=\"fn\">dir</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine\">Machine</a> <span class=\"fn\">dir</span></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Prod\">×</a> <a href=\"./Std/Http/Internal/ChunkedBuffer.html#Std.Http.Internal.ChunkedBuffer\">Internal.ChunkedBuffer</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Takes and clears accumulated output bytes, returning them as a buffer.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.takeOutput","kind":"def","line":1279,"name":"Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.takeOutput","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Protocol/H1.lean#L1279-L1285"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.takeEvents\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Protocol</span>.<span class=\"name\">H1</span>.<span class=\"name\">Machine</span>.<span class=\"name\">takeEvents</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">dir</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Message.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Direction\">Direction</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">machine</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine\">Machine</a> <span class=\"fn\">dir</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine\">Machine</a> <span class=\"fn\">dir</span></span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Prod\">×</a> <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Array\">Array</a> <span class=\"fn\">(<a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Event.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Event\">Event</a> <span class=\"fn\">dir</span>)</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Takes and clears all accumulated events, returning the drained array.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.takeEvents","kind":"def","line":1272,"name":"Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.takeEvents","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Protocol/H1.lean#L1272-L1277"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.closeWithError\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Protocol</span>.<span class=\"name\">H1</span>.<span class=\"name\">Machine</span>.<span class=\"name\">closeWithError</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">machine</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine\">Machine</a> <a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Message.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Direction.receiving\">Direction.receiving</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">status</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/Status.html#Std.Http.Status\">Status</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine\">Machine</a> <a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Message.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Direction.receiving\">Direction.receiving</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Sends an error response with `Connection: close` and shuts down input.\n\nIf the machine is waiting to send a message, sends `status` with a `Connection: close`\nheader and a short `text/plain` explanation (letting the step function encode and flush the\nresponse), then stops accepting further input. Otherwise, closes the writer directly, ends\nkeep-alive and stops accepting further input.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.closeWithError","kind":"def","line":1256,"name":"Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.closeWithError","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Protocol/H1.lean#L1256-L1270"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.canContinue\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Protocol</span>.<span class=\"name\">H1</span>.<span class=\"name\">Machine</span>.<span class=\"name\">canContinue</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">dir</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Message.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Direction\">Direction</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">machine</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine\">Machine</a> <span class=\"fn\">dir</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">status</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/Status.html#Std.Http.Status\">Status</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine\">Machine</a> <span class=\"fn\">dir</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Resolves an `Expect: 100-continue` decision.\n\nWhen `status` is `100 Continue`, sends the interim response and advances to body\nreading. For any other status, sends the rejection response (typically 417) with a short\n`text/plain` explanation, unless a final response was already sent, disables keep-alive, and closes\nthe reader — the body will not be received.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.canContinue","kind":"def","line":1232,"name":"Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.canContinue","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Protocol/H1.lean#L1232-L1254"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.sendData\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Protocol</span>.<span class=\"name\">H1</span>.<span class=\"name\">Machine</span>.<span class=\"name\">sendData</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">dir</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Message.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Direction\">Direction</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">machine</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine\">Machine</a> <span class=\"fn\">dir</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">data</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Array\">Array</a> <a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/Chunk.html#Std.Http.Chunk\">Chunk</a></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine\">Machine</a> <span class=\"fn\">dir</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Enqueues body chunks into the writer buffer for encoding and sending.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.sendData","kind":"def","line":1202,"name":"Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.sendData","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Protocol/H1.lean#L1202-L1212"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.send\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Protocol</span>.<span class=\"name\">H1</span>.<span class=\"name\">Machine</span>.<span class=\"name\">send</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">dir</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Message.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Direction\">Direction</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">machine</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine\">Machine</a> <span class=\"fn\">dir</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">message</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Message.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Message.Head\">Message.Head</a> <span class=\"fn\"><span class=\"fn\">dir</span>.<a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Message.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Direction.swap\">swap</a></span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine\">Machine</a> <span class=\"fn\">dir</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Send the head of a message to the machine.\n\nMust only be called when `machine.isWaitingMessage` is true. If called in any\nother state (e.g. called twice), the machine panics.\n\nInformational (1xx) responses are written directly to the output buffer, or dropped when the\nrequest is HTTP/1.0; the writer stays in `waitingHeaders` so the application can send additional\ninterim responses or the final response. The reader state is not affected — use `canContinue` to\nresolve an `Expect: 100-continue` decision separately.\n\nA `Content-Length` in the head gives the length of a body set as `chunked`, whose length is unknown.\nA head whose `Content-Length` or `Transfer-Encoding` otherwise contradicts the length set with\n`setKnownSize`, or describes no length, is not written: a server answers `500 Internal Server\nError` and closes the connection, and a client ends the exchange. Both emit `.failed` with an\n`.other` error, set `error` and close the reader, so the machine halts.\nA response without content (to `HEAD`, or a 204, 205 or 304) cannot contradict it, and a HEAD response\nadvertises the `Content-Length` of its head.\n\nA message HTTP/1.0 cannot frame (see `unframeableForHttp10`) is rejected the same way. A 2xx to\n`CONNECT` is written without content or framing fields, and the connection then closes.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.send","kind":"def","line":1124,"name":"Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.send","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Protocol/H1.lean#L1124-L1200"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.suppressOutgoingBody\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Protocol</span>.<span class=\"name\">H1</span>.<span class=\"name\">Machine</span>.<span class=\"name\">suppressOutgoingBody</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">dir</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Message.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Direction\">Direction</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">machine</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine\">Machine</a> <span class=\"fn\">dir</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">forceZero</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a> := <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.false\">false</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine\">Machine</a> <span class=\"fn\">dir</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Suppresses writing body bytes for the current outgoing message while keeping\nheader generation active. Used for responses that must not carry payload bytes.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.suppressOutgoingBody","kind":"def","line":981,"name":"Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.suppressOutgoingBody","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Protocol/H1.lean#L981-L993"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.setKnownSize\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">Protocol</span>.<span class=\"name\">H1</span>.<span class=\"name\">Machine</span>.<span class=\"name\">setKnownSize</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">dir</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1/Message.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Direction\">Direction</a>}</span></span> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">machine</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine\">Machine</a> <span class=\"fn\">dir</span></span>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">size</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/Body/Length.html#Std.Http.Body.Length\">Body.Length</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine\">Machine</a> <span class=\"fn\">dir</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Set a known size for the message body, replacing any previous value.","docLink":"./Std/Http/Protocol/H1.html#Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.setKnownSize","kind":"def","line":974,"name":"Std.Http.Protocol.H1.Machine.setKnownSize","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Std/Http/Protocol/H1.lean#L97